==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|get<,,got,got[UK]:gotten[US]> across}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|intransitive}} To [[cross#Verb|cross]]; to [[move#Verb|move]] from one side (of something) to the other, literally or figuratively.
#: {{ux|en|In heavy rain, the cavalry couldn't '''get across''' the river.}}
#: {{ux|en|It's impossible to '''get across''' with all checkpoints closed.}}
#: {{ux|en|Bridge the digital divide. Let the poor '''get across'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make an idea [[evident]]; to successfully [[explain]] a thought or feeling; [[put over]].
#: {{ux|en|I couldn't '''get across''' to the board this simple economic fact.}}
#: {{ux|en|Better organized writing helps to '''get''' the point '''across'''.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|slang|AAVE|dated}} To succeed; to do well.
# {{lb|en|transitive|slang}} To [[annoy]] (someone); to get on someone's bad side.

